Byomkesh asked no more questions, closing his eyes as if sinking into meditation. Suddenly, I remembered—yesterday morning, when Mrs. Ushapati entered the room unexpectedly, he had stared at her in astonishment. At the time, I hadn’t understood the meaning of that look. …Has the long estrangement between husband and wife been mended by the death of their son?

Even after Shitanshu left, Byomkesh sat for a long time with his eyes closed. Then, with a sigh, he opened them. “A tragic affair. —What did you think of Shitanshu?”
“I think he was telling the truth.”
“The boy is clever—very clever.” With that, he lapsed into contemplation again.

Half an hour later, his reverie was broken by a knock at the outer door. I rose and went to the door.

