“It takes at least half an hour to sing a single pad. I had just finished Jagadananda’s ‘Manju Bikach Kusum-Punj’ when the telephone rang in the next room. Before I could get up, he went and answered it. Two minutes later, he returned and said, ‘I have to go at once—Hena has fallen from the roof and died.’  
He left immediately, in the same attire he was wearing.”  

When Sukumari fell silent, Byomkesh too remained quiet for a while. At last he asked, “You don’t know who made the telephone call?”  
Sukumari replied, “No. Afterwards, I inquired in this house, but no one here had made the call.”  
