Byomkesh looked around and asked, “You know everyone in the house. Can you tell me what kind of people they are?”

Medini paused for a moment, picking at her fingernails, then replied, “The old master was a very good man, a generous soul. His son and son-in-law are good men too. The daughter and daughter-in-law do not like me. Jhillī-di and Laboni-di are very nice women.”

