He then knocked on Sanat’s door. Sanat opened it, an English detective novel in his hand, pages half-turned. Seeing Rakhalbabu, he said, “Inspectorbabu, I’ve run out of cigarettes. Could you have a tin brought for me? Gold Flake.”

“Certainly. Give me the money, I’ll have it fetched.”

Sanat pulled a ten-rupee note from his pocket and handed it over. Rakhalbabu gave the note to the sub-inspector and said, “Go to the shop out front and fetch a tin of Gold Flake cigarettes.”

He entered the room with Byomkesh. Sanat said, “How much longer will you keep me locked up in here? My work is piling up. Besides, now that uncle has died, his heirs won’t let me stay here much longer. I’ll have to find a place to put my head.”

“How do you know they won’t let you stay?”

