“Is that so!—Well, you won’t be inconvenienced much longer. In a day or two, you’ll be free. This is Byomkesh Bakshi, the renowned satyanweshi.”

Sanat glanced at Byomkesh with indifferent eyes and said in a flat tone, “I’ve heard the name, but never read the books. I don’t read Bengali detective stories. —Please, sit.”

Byomkesh’s eyes wandered lazily around the room. He asked, “Do you have a raincoat?”

Sanat raised an eyebrow in mild surprise. “Yes. But it’s not the rainy season, so I’ve put it away. Would you like to see it?”

“Yes.”

