At four in the afternoon, Rakhalbabu called—‘Everything’s arranged. Bring a suitcase and come straight to the station.’  

In Byomkesh’s absence, the routine at Benimadhab’s house continued as before. No one was permitted to leave. A sub-inspector, a jamadar, and four constables remained on constant duty. Rakhalbabu came twice a day to inspect the premises. No new information came to light regarding Benimadhab’s death. Medini’s makeup box, once vanished, remained missing.  

One day, Laboni came to visit her parents, accompanied by her husband. Rakhalbabu allowed them to meet. What transpired behind closed doors as the Ajay family welcomed their daughter and son-in-law remained unknown. When Laboni emerged, her face was wreathed in smiles, her eyes brimming with tears. In the veranda, she met Jhilli; the two sisters embraced, kissed each other, and then—

