Hand in hand, they descended the stairs. Nikhil was waiting on the lower verandah; seeing the newlyweds, he burst out laughing and said, “Ah, here come the fugitives! The runaway bride and groom! The two of you have been dancing up quite a storm, haven’t you?”

With a mock melancholy, Parag replied, “Dancing together? Where’s that happening? Right now, I’m the one dancing, and Laboni is making me dance.”

After Laboni and her party had left, Nikhil turned to Jhillī and said, “Well, what are you waiting for? One’s already run off with a dancer—now it’s your turn to slip away with a singer.”

